# {{ project_name }} Design

## Current state

Freshly stamped from the household's canonical full-stack template. The
frontend consumes `@poodle64/design-tokens` and `@poodle64/ui` as shipped —
no local overrides beyond the primary accent below.

## Shared baseline

The household shared design language and token package are the binding
sources for any UI work in this repo:

- **Design language doc:** `docs/master/reference/guide-shared-design-language.md`
- **Token package:** `@poodle64/design-tokens` (public npm, from `kits/typescript`
  in `radar-hooves/app-factory`)
- **Component package:** `@poodle64/ui` — the shadcn-svelte primitives plus
  the composed `AppShell` every app builds its routes from
  (`rules-library/stacks/sveltekit-frontend.md`)

The package defines the binding constants for radius (`--ds-radius-lg:
0.625rem`), typography (Fraunces display; Avenir Next, else Hanken Grotesk,
body; JetBrains Mono code), status vocabulary (success / warning / error /
info / neutral), colour space (oklch), and the `--ds-*` namespace.

## Brand primary

`app.css` overrides `--ds-color-primary` only — everything else in the shared
token sheet is used as-is. Stamped default: Eucalyptus (hue 145). Pick your
own hue by changing the three `oklch(...)` values in `:root` and `.dark` (see
the comment inline).

## Shell

`src/lib/app-frame.svelte` wraps every route under `routes/(protected)/` in
`AppShell`: one composition in every app, a side rail (a drawer on a phone)
and a top bar, with no variant to choose. The frame declares the app's `nav`
and hands the same value to the rail and the command palette. A route says
how wide its page may get, and whether it pads itself, in its load data:

```ts
// routes/(protected)/reports/+layout.ts
import type { LayoutLoad } from './$types';
export const load: LayoutLoad = () => ({ measure: 'page' });
```

`measure` is `prose`, `page`, `wide` (the frame's default) or `full`; `padded`
defaults to true. The content texture is on by default. Sidebar and chart
colours are the one surface the package leaves to each app, declared and
registered in `app.css` alongside the primary override.

## Pages

Every route builds from the same parts, all from `@poodle64/ui`:

| Part | Component |
| --- | --- |
| The page, at one rhythm | `PageContainer` |
| Its title, trail, facts and actions | `PageHeader` (`breadcrumbs={[{ label, href }]}`) |
| A section of it | `PageSection` |
| A titled card | `Panel` |
| A document to read | `DocumentReader` |
| A region still loading | `ContentSkeleton`; a whole page waiting is `LoadingState` |
| A panel over the page from an edge | `Sheet` |

The type scale, by role:

| Role | Utility | Size | Face |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Page title | `text-display` | 1.75rem | display, semibold |
| Section | `text-section` | 1.25rem | display, semibold |
| Panel title, subsection | `text-body` | 0.9375rem | body, semibold |
| Reading text | `text-base` | 1rem | body |
| Body | `text-sm` | 0.875rem | body |
| Facts, captions | `text-xs` | 0.75rem | body, muted |
| Column head | `text-2xs`, uppercase | 0.6875rem | body, medium |

A route sets no size of its own; it composes the component that owns the role.

## Adoption path

To change the accent colour:

1. Edit the `--ds-color-primary` (and `--ds-color-ring`) values in
   `frontend/src/app.css`.
2. Update this file's `status` frontmatter field once the identity is settled.
